    "summary": "Somali Police Force Commander Gen. Asad Osman Abdullahi concluded a leadership and management training for senior officers, delivered by EUCAP experts, focusing on modern strategies and technology use.",
    "content": "The Commander of the Somali Police Force, Major General Asad Osman Abdullahi, officially closed a training program on good leadership and management for senior officers of the force on Wednesday. The training was conducted by experts from the European Union Capacity Building Mission (EUCAP) in Somalia. The program, held in Mogadishu, aimed to strengthen the leadership capabilities of senior police officials.\n\nThe training focused on contemporary strategies and techniques related to administration and leadership. According to officials, the sessions emphasized adapting to global changes, particularly advancements in technology and how to leverage them for policing. Participants were drawn from various ranks within the Somali Police Force.\n\nThis initiative is part of ongoing efforts by the Somali government and international partners to professionalize the country's security forces. EUCAP has been actively involved in training and advising Somali police since 2012. The mission works to enhance the capacity of Somali law enforcement to maintain security and uphold the rule of law.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the development of a professional and accountable police force is crucial. Many diaspora members have family and business interests in Somalia and closely follow security sector reforms. A well-trained police force can contribute to improved safety and stability, which are key factors for diaspora investment and return. The emphasis on modern leadership and technology also signals a shift toward more effective and transparent policing.\n\nSuch training programs are seen as vital for building public trust in the police. By equipping senior officers with modern management skills, the initiative aims to improve the overall effectiveness of the force. The Somali Police Force continues to face significant challenges, including security threats and institutional capacity gaps. International support remains a cornerstone of efforts to address these challenges.\n\nThe closing ceremony was attended by senior police officials and representatives from EUCAP. The Commander expressed appreciation for the EU's continued support and urged participants to apply their new skills in their daily duties.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/08/taliyaha-booliiska-soomaaliyeed-oo-soo-xiray-tababar-ku-saabsan-hoggaaminta-iyo-maamulka/",
